35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Oh no! I found out that some people in the outer wards have a really hard time getting to us now because of the buses!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the ghosts of our past are speaking. We've had outreach success before, though we managed to let some of it slip through our fingers.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"How predictable. We have a list of volunteers, but absolutely no one on the staff who knows how to manage them or maintain the equipment.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,The financial data is revealing. We are losing money on operations while returning capital funds. The funding structure is fundamentally mismatched with our needs.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I saw the same thing about the buses. And the roads north of the river close a lot in winter, but the local halls stay open.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, you're right! If we rely on the roads, we'll fail in winter. We need a plan that doesn't break when the weather changes!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. If we look at the outreach data, the demand is there, but our internal management—as Shion noted—is a disaster.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,It's more than a disaster; it's a void. We are proposing expansions while the person who knew how to certify the tools is gone. We're flying blind.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"If we choose a proposal that relies on high operational costs but low initial capital, we will be bankrupt by year two. We must choose a sustainable model.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Maybe... maybe we shouldn't make people come to us? If the buses are gone, they just... they can't reach us.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"That's a wonderful idea, Daisuke! Let's find a way to bring the library to them, but in a way that doesn't depend on the roads!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A ""mobile"" service that isn't actually mobile during winter. How paradoxical. We should look for a proposal that utilizes existing community hubs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, you're finally making sense. But remember, if we use hubs, we still need someone to supervise them. We can't just dump work on the staff.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I agree. A hub-based model reduces the reliance on the vehicle running lines, which we know are currently over-budget and unstable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just... I don't want anyone to be left out because of where they live.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm so glad we're all thinking about this! I just want everyone to be happy and have access to books, no matter what!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Your enthusiasm is almost as infectious as the inefficiency of our previous digitisation project. Let us hope the candidates reflect this logic.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,Let's just hope the candidates aren't as delusional as the people who wrote the current staff roster.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"Let us remain focused. We need a proposal that is operationally lean, utilizes existing hubs, and fits the grant structure.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I hope so too.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
