60,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh! I think Option C is the best! It uses partner organizations, so it won't stop just because a road is closed or a bus is cancelled!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option C is the only one that doesn't ignore the lessons of the past. We've tried the ""centralized"" approach and the ""mobile"" approach; community hubs are the logical path.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is a death trap. We have no one to certify the tools. Option D is a logistical nightmare given the road closures. C is the only one that doesn't require a miracle.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option D is financially unsustainable given the vehicle running costs. Option A requires too much capital for a one-off. Option C distributes the operational burden.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think Option C is good. It means people don't have to travel to the main branch... and they can meet in their own neighborhoods.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Yumi,,See! Everyone agrees! It's so wonderful when we can all find a way to help everyone together!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a rare moment of alignment. Usually, we spend more time debating the aesthetics of the plan than the actual feasibility of the execution.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Don't get too excited, Yumi. It's not about ""helping everyone""; it's about the fact that the other options are logically impossible given our current failures.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Regardless of the motivation, the conclusion is the same. Option C is the only proposal that aligns with the funding structure and the physical constraints of the region.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I'm just... I'm glad we're not choosing the mobile bus. I was worried about the winter roads.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, we've got this! We're making a choice that's strong and steady! I'm so happy we're doing this!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall cast my vote for C. It is the only choice that doesn't feel like a repeat of a failed experiment from six years ago.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,I'll vote for C as well. It's the only one that doesn't assume the staff can magically perform tasks they aren't trained for.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,I concur. Option C is the most fiscally responsible and operationally viable choice.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'll vote for C too. It feels... right.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Yumi,,Me too! Option C it is! Yay!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
